  "Specification": "This module is a parser and definability test for user-defined operators written with many infix and prefix symbolic forms in TLA+. It defines a large collection of custom operators, mostly binary and a few unary, and then uses ASSUME statements to assert that those operators can also be invoked in prefix form such as +(4, 6), \\leq(4, 6), or \\in(1, {1}). The file does not model a transition system, has no variables or temporal behavior, and instead serves as a syntax-oriented validation of operator definitions, operator application notation, and a few built-in symbolic forms like \\in, \\cup, \\X, and \\o.",
